From cec59fa8afcc27b72dabc63e976782e7b0d6021b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fengshuai <shuai.feng@sunmi.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 11:28:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 04/13] feat(llm): request-size gate and 413 image-offload
 recovery

- llm: add isRequestTooLargeError, the shared provider-neutral predicate
  for transport byte-size rejections (HTTP 413), kept disjoint from
  context-window overflow wording
- llm-pi-ai: optional per-route maxRequestBytes; the projected request
  body (history, tools, and retained images at exact request bytes,
  conservatively padded) is checked before serialization, failing with
  IMAGE_OFFLOAD_REQUIRED while offloading oldest images still fits the
  bound and with INVALID_REQUEST once even the image-free remainder no
  longer fits; 413 stream failures now name the remaining recovery
  actions instead of surfacing the raw status line
- compaction-image-offload: a provider-side size rejection whose wording
  matches the too-large predicate offloads half the retained input-image
  occurrences and retries, converging within logarithmically many
  attempts; it steps aside once nothing remains to offload
